    "highlights": "Inline text highlights use bold red (#ff2d09) applied to specific strong phrases or words to draw attention within hero text (e.g., .hero-intro__highlight, .hero-title__highlight).",
    "insights": [
      "The typography system relies heavily on a single core sans-serif typeface (Helvetica) styled functionally, giving the site a clean, unopinionated, and academic 'research lab' feel.",
      "Display typography is characterized by extremely tight line-heights (0.95 - 1.05) and negative letter-spacing for maximum visual density, while body copy prioritizes readability with generous line-heights (1.6+).",
      "Multiple monospace fonts (SF Mono, Berkeley Mono, ui-monospace) are specified exclusively for code blocks and academic citations (BibTeX), directly catering to a highly technical audience."
